# K1 semantic challenge round 1: 18 frozen samples.
1 UPHELD | Checking that a value belongs in the file is GOV-008 and GOV-011 applied; no extra duty.
2 UPHELD | The source restates RUN-010, and 'verify the changed files' adds nothing beyond removing the imports.
3 UPHELD | Tagged Default and restates GOV-005.
4 UPHELD | 'Typical' gives guidance under ARC-028, and the source's opening sentence owns the MUST NOT; the checker's allow-list is read at its own record.
5 UPHELD | An arbitrary delay works against determinism in TST-004; 'avoid' is below the MUST, so WEAKER with GR is right.
6 REVISED_NEEDED | 'A simple Domain needs no dedicated test project' is not entailed: a useful Domain.Tests project is not speculative under ARC-027. FG-K1-0e4de41164 already reads the same sentence as XP inside K1. Corrected by COR-K1-0001.
7 UPHELD | A size warning on an instruction artifact; WF-010 does not limit file size.
8 UPHELD | Slot definition and fixed skill name are instruction architecture; the framework consistency check is read at the facet.
9 UPHELD | Surfacing a missing contract item during a slot replacement is instruction-system procedure, with ARC-020 only related.
10 UPHELD | DEP-021 says nothing on flushing; a static logger with no flush satisfies it, so the scenario distinguishes.
11 UPHELD | These settings are not in RUN-009's own text; a repository without them still satisfies it.
12 UPHELD | This source says 'do not duplicate', so MUST NOT stands; API-010 and FE-010 do not forbid repeating a rule for an optional preview, so the scenario distinguishes.
13 UPHELD | NUnit restates TST-001; the assertion style is not in the policy, and classic assertions satisfy it.
14 UPHELD | Agrees with the calibration: the checker has no explicit-request branch for floating versions, and exact bracket pins are also errors.
15 UPHELD | API-014 lets a new version ship without approval; K1 reserves any breaking public change.
16 UPHELD | The subclauses are separable: one is a preference and the other a library limit under GOV-013 and DEP-001.
17 UPHELD | DEP-011 approves Mapster when warranted; ARC-002 names no mapping library, so the Domain limit is a real remainder.
18 UPHELD | The placement is RUN-009 adjacent product configuration; the preference about instruction text is instruction architecture.
